WEBVTT

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:03.476
Reframing is a process of finding some

00:00:03.516 --> 00:00:07.090
positive aspects
of a perceived negative event.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:12.450
This may also include seeing some
kind of benefit in a bad situation.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.990
It is highly useful as a coping skill.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:21.510
Some researchers have studied when people
are able to reframe traumatic experiences.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.890
They call this post-traumatic growth.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:30.630
Post-traumatic growth involves positive
shifts after experiencing great trauma.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:35.125
For some people, tinnitus
symptoms have been traumatic.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:39.130
But will you let tinnitus define
you or determine your happiness?

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:45.110
If not, then you can use reframing to help
shift your outlook to be more positive.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:48.430
An example of reframing is the following.

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:52.910
You have tinnitus and it cannot
be cured at this point in time.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:56.277
Yet, there may be some
positive aspects or events

00:00:56.317 --> 00:00:59.910
that have been a result
of your having tinnitus.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:05.015
For example, some people have said that having
tinnitus made them more compassionate

00:01:05.055 --> 00:01:09.870
about the suffering of others and more
aware about the fragility of life.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:13.610
Some appreciate the caring that they
received from medical staff,

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:16.356
audiologists, and other
health care providers.

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:19.223
Some are more aware of how
their spouses, family,

00:01:19.263 --> 00:01:24.610
or friends supported and cared about them
when they started dealing with tinnitus.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.390
These examples of reframing
reflect that while

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:31.041
the stress of tinnitus has not changed,

00:01:31.081 --> 00:01:37.510
other aspects of your life may improve
even if you cannot change your tinnitus.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:43.130
Many of us let the negative events
in our lives dominate our thinking.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:46.184
It is even more difficult to spot
the positive aspects of our

00:01:46.224 --> 00:01:49.096
lives when we have chronic health
conditions such as tinnitus

00:01:49.136 --> 00:01:52.630
that do not leave us alone
and from which we cannot escape.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:57.239
But with greater awareness of what our
minds are focusing on and by intentionally

00:01:57.279 --> 00:02:00.720
seeking out and planning positive
events and working on reframing

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:04.243
our focus on negative aspects
of our lives, we can start shifting

00:02:04.283 --> 00:02:08.090
the focus away from a constant
bombardment of negative thoughts.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:11.692
When we start shifting from a heavy
focus on the negative issues

00:02:11.732 --> 00:02:15.596
that occur in our lives, we may
experience less of the fight-or-flight

00:02:15.636 --> 00:02:19.290
mode that is associated
with heightened stress levels.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:23.470
We are drawing to the end of this course.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.547
We have talked about many
ideas in these sections,

00:02:26.587 --> 00:02:31.950
some of them you may have already known
while others may have been new to you.

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:34.718
The goal of this course was
to provide a structured,

00:02:34.758 --> 00:02:37.830
organized format for you
to think about coping.

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:42.040
You may have been familiar with some
or even most of this information,

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:45.470
but hopefully it was
presented in a new way to you.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:49.810
The major take-home points
of this course are the following.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.759
1. Modify your sound
environment so that your brain

00:02:53.799 --> 00:02:56.570
pays less attention
to your tinnitus symptoms.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:02.152
2. Understand how to use the three
main types of coping strategies,

00:03:02.192 --> 00:03:05.730
problem solving, stress management,
and social support.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:11.294
3. Integrate your knowledge of these three
types of coping strategies with the types

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:15.746
of stress you are dealing with, that is,
changeable or unchangeable stress.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.865
Match or fit the type of coping strategy

00:03:17.905 --> 00:03:21.170
that is most appropriate
for the type of stress.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.799
4. In the parallel way that you
should add to your sound

00:03:25.839 --> 00:03:28.900
environment to decrease
your brain's focus on tinnitus,

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:32.330
you should try to intentionally
add positive events, thoughts,

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:37.550
and practices to your life in order to
decrease your focus on the negative aspects,

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.250
such as having tinnitus.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:45.290
Unfortunately, at this time,
most forms of tinnitus are unchangeable.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:49.590
This does NOT mean you have
to suffer when you have tinnitus.

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:54.285
Coping strategies emphasize that you
should attempt to intentionally change what

00:03:54.325 --> 00:03:59.030
is stressful to you, and this can be
done by using problem-solving strategies.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:00.809
But when that is not possible,

00:04:00.849 --> 00:04:05.236
you can change your response to the stress
by using multiple types of stress

00:04:05.276 --> 00:04:09.570
management and social support
strategies as covered in this course.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:12.050
There are many more possibilities.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.910
You are only limited by your imagination.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:18.664
We would like to invite
you to take the same coping

00:04:18.704 --> 00:04:21.650
assessment that you took
at the beginning of this course.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.945
You will be able to see
if there is a difference

00:04:23.985 --> 00:04:26.770
in your scores after
finishing this assessment.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:31.522
You can provide feedback about
the content of this course

00:04:31.562 --> 00:04:38.490
by emailing the course instructors
at rehabilityllc at gmail.com.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:42.430
Thank you for taking
time to learn from us.
